<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  DEBUG-ONLY network security policy.

  Android blocks cleartext HTTP by default (targetSdk >= 28). Dev stacks are
  served over plain http — on the Mac's loopback via `adb reverse`, on its LAN
  address, or on whatever machine runs the backend that week — so a debug build
  must be allowed to talk to them, or Settings → Server can point the app at an
  origin it then cannot reach ("java.net.UnknownServiceException: CLEARTEXT
  communication to … not permitted by network security policy").

  Shape of the policy, and why it changed:

    - `base-config` permits cleartext. Settings → Server accepts a CUSTOM origin,
      so an allowlist of known dev hosts cannot be complete by construction: the
      previous fixed list (localhost / 127.0.0.1 / ::1 / 10.0.2.2 / 192.168.0.114)
      broke silently the moment the dev box moved to another address, and the
      failure looks like "the app is broken", not "the policy refused it".

    - The OFFICIAL BetterTrack hosts keep cleartext refused, explicitly. That is
      the half of the old rationale worth keeping: not even a debug build may
      downgrade the real backend to plain http, whatever is typed into the
      Server screen.

  This file lives in `app/src/debug/` and is referenced by the debug-only
  manifest overlay, so it is NOT part of any release artifact: a release build —
  including `githubRelease`, which ships the Server screen — keeps the platform
  default of "all cleartext refused". That is deliberate and stays: the Server
  screen says in words that http works on debug builds only, and an https custom
  origin works everywhere.
-->
<network-security-config xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <!--
      InsecureBaseConfiguration is exactly what this line is, and it is the
      point: this file is merged into DEBUG builds only, and the official hosts
      are excluded below. Suppressed with the reason attached so nobody
      "fixes" it back into an allowlist that a moved dev box breaks again.
    -->
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" tools:ignore="InsecureBaseConfiguration" />

    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">bettertrack.at</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
